# Naming conventions (Envy)

## Classes / structs
- MFC classes: `C` + PascalCase (e.g., `CDownloadTask`)
- Plain structs: PascalCase (e.g., `FileMetadata`)

## Member prefixes (actual codebase)
- `m_s*`: strings (`CString`, `CStringList`) **(hard rule: use `m_s`, not `m_str`)**
- `m_n*`: numbers/sizes/counts
- `m_b*`: booleans (**use `BOOL` for MFC members**)
- `m_p*`: pointers (raw or smart pointers)
- `m_h*`: handles (`HANDLE`, `SOCKET`, hooks)
- `m_t*`: time/tick values
- `m_o*`: object/collection members

## Locals / parameters
- Use short type-prefix locals when it improves clarity: `str`, `n`, `b`, `p`, `h`, `t`, `o`.
- Avoid single-letter names except loop counters (`i`, `j`, `k`).

## Functions / methods
- Methods: PascalCase (public + private).
- MFC handlers: `On...` (e.g., `OnBnClickedOk`, `OnTimer`, `OnSize`).

## Files
- Prefer file names that match the primary class: `Foo.h` / `Foo.cpp`.
- Related helpers: `FooHelpers.cpp`, `FooTests.cpp` (only when it improves navigation).
